{"name":"Shore","hex":"#81d5c6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Shore","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A topographic surname from Middle English.","A place in England:\nA suburb of Littleborough, Metropolitan Borough of Rochdale, Greater Manchester . \nA hamlet near Cornholme in Todmorden parish, Calderdale borough, West Yorkshire ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Shore"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shore (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Shore is the fourth studio album by American band Fleet Foxes, released on September 22, 2020, by Anti- Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e3/Shore_%28Fleet_Foxes%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shore_(album)"},{"title":"Coast","blocks":[{"text":"A coast is the land next to the sea or the line that forms the boundary between the land and the ocean or a lake. Coasts are influenced by the topography of the surrounding landscape and by aquatic erosion, such as that caused by waves. The geological composition of rock and soil dictates the type of shore that is created. Earth has about 620,000.0 km (385,250.1 mi) of coastline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg/330px-Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coast"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lake_Minnewaska_from_cliffs.jpg/500px-Lake_Minnewaska_from_cliffs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lake_Minnewaska_from_cliffs.jpg/1280px-Lake_Minnewaska_from_cliffs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co